		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=29721#p29721"><![CDATA[
I am not sure about your effective mass calculation. Looks weird. It should be:<br>Kn = InvM1 + InvM2 + ( r1 x n )^T * InvI1 * ( r1 x n ) + ( r2 x n )^T * InvI2 * ( r2 x n ) + <br><br>You can implement v^T * A * v as Dot( v, A * v ) where A * v is matrix times vector.<br>The effective mass can be computed the same for friction constraints. Just swap n with your tangent vector.<br><br>For the tangent creation look into btPlaneSpace(). You can search the forum for this. I commented on this before.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Fri Jan 18, 2013 4:01 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
